#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: params bio
#: content/authors/dustinjacobus/_index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Through art rooted in solarpunk and eco-futurism, I challenge systems of harm and envision a world where all species are protected and valued."
msgstr "Dustin Jacobus is an illustrator and industrial design engineer whose work explores how nature and the built environment can grow together."

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#: content/authors/dustinjacobus/_index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Dustin Jacobus"
msgstr "ዳስቲን ጃኮቡስ"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/authors/dustinjacobus/_index.en.md
msgid ""
"Dustin Jacobus is an illustrator and industrial design engineer whose work "
"explores how nature and the built environment can grow together. Deeply "
"inspired by natural systems, his art is rooted in biomimicry, sustainable "
"design, and the solarpunk movement. He envisions a world where we coexist in "
"harmony with all life forms, creating sustainable, water-rich, and green "
"environments, both urban and beyond and expresses these ideas through his "
"art. His vision has been shared in exhibitions, talks, workshops, and a wide "
"range of publications across books, magazines, and other media."
msgstr ""
"Deeply inspired by natural systems, his art is rooted in biomimicry, "
"sustainable design, and the solarpunk movement. He envisions a world where "
"we coexist in harmony with all life forms, creating sustainable, water-rich, "
"and green environments, both urban and beyond and expresses these ideas "
"through his art. His vision has been shared in exhibitions, talks, "
"workshops, and a wide range of publications across books, magazines, and "
"other media."

